% n17: an inductive with a constructor whose domain is an UNBOUND variable.
% The inductive type's domain can refer to inductive types, but a constructor's
% pi domain must be a type; an unbound de Bruijn var at index 0 is not.
% The kernel prints 0 (accepts); the twin rejects with code 20 (var unbound).
1 sort 0
2 var 0
3 const Foo
4 pi 2 3
inductive Foo : 1 | ctor : 4
